I ascended after playing for three monthes, thanks to this list and
lots of spoilers.

I started the game with 15 daggers and 16 constitution, which made me
quite cheerful. I was playing semi-pacifist so I manage to get to
Minetown at XLVL 3. A general store yielded an expensive lamp, but none
at Izchaks. B/u/c testing the lamp, it comes out to be blessed. So
naturally I wished up GDSM. The Minetown has the bones of a past me,
which died from a white unicorn. I let my large cat, which I
impersonally name Cat1, maul the unicorn then sacrificed it and took
the horn. The bones had +0 boots of speed, +0 shield of reflection,
assorted rings, two bags of holding, and a wand of enlightenment I
id'd by engraving. The wand turned out to be VERY handy, because I
found out the gray stone I found was a luck stone, and also that I had
a =oConflict, =oFreeaction, and =oTC. The tool shop had a magic marker
and stethoscope, both of which I grabbed. Since I got a luck stone I
decided to skip the rest of Minetown. Sokoban had the AoR I was hoping
for. I switched that for the shield so I could #twoweapon my two
dwarvish shortswords. I id'd both scrolls of enchant armor and
weapon. So my dagger stack got to +4 and my GDSM became +5. The mid
game was a breeze thanks to my magic whistle. My first tame dog became
Wormie the purple worm, my second tame dog became Blubie the blue
dragon, my first cat became Fishface the water elemental, and my second
cat died. During a sacfest to get my luck up (I was hoping to avoid
getting artifacts so I could wish for Grayswandir) the scroll of create
monster created about 15 monsters. So I read my blessed scroll of
taming and got even more pets. Unfortunately my companionship is pretty
dangerous and after a while it's just me, Wormie, Fishface, and my
unnamed silver dragon. By the time I got to Medusa I was XLVL 5 and
Wormie was XLVL 25 with 250 health. Along the way I found the Bones of
a monk who died from a brigade of soldiers. He had +2 gloves of dex,
which came in handy, but not much else. I did a little scroll writing
and got my armor class to around -17. I dug down from medusa because I
had a lack of levitation and got to the castle. Then I realize I
didn't have either an instrument or a method of breaking down the
drawbridge. Crap! I knew I should have taken those wands of striking
which I left at my stash. I went back up and killed medusa (I was
permanently invisible, so I had to whack her to death) and zapped my
wand of cold from island to island. Then I noticed that I had a potion
of levitation. Duh! So I went up got the /oStriking and smashed the
drawbridge down. And then I remember I have no levitation or cold left.
I read the sokoban ?oEarth to make myself a path. Playing like this I
was sort of worried about my survival. Cleared out the castle without
having to use conflict thanks to my pets and got the wand. I wished for
boots of levitation, and Grayswandir (I was worried I wouldn't get it
since Grimtooth, String, and Orcrist had all been generated) then the
remaining wishes went to scrolls and magic markers. I nursed danced and
succumbi danced to get to XLVL 14 and a lot of health. Thanks to large
leprechaun halls I paid the priest of moloch until I stopped receiving
protection, then paid then paid her for clairvoyance then had her
killed by my pets. I took the robes and her spell books. Detect monster
was very handy and magic missile replaced my dagger stack which was
eaten by a xorn. I made the mistake of taking my pets to my quest
because they ate the chameleons and turned into dumb monsters. I was
really annoyed that Wormie polyed into a panther, but I couldn't help
it now. I got really nervous because I had cursed scrolls of
teleportation I was going to use to get to the Master Assassin, but I
was typing 19 instead of 4 to try and get to Home 4 and so I wasted two
scrolls. Luckily though I got into the right place with one scroll
remaining. The Master Assassin wasn't too difficult and so I took the
M Key of Thievery and left. I tamed a new purple worm who became
Buuuuuurp and turned Wormie into Crossbones the bone devil. Now it's
time for Gehonnem. I found the vibrating square and marked it then
cleared all but the top level of the wizard's tower. I had a
misconception that Vlad's tower couldn't be generated on a
Wizard's tower level, so it took me around 10k turns just to find it.
The only reason I did find it was because I read a scroll of amnesia
and had to remap that level. Vlad was a wimp like others had reported
and a wand of death took out Rodney. I almost left the tower without
taking the book, but remembered as I was crossing the moat. I do a
little preparation then perform the invocation. A wand of secret door
detection made finding the door easy and I took the Priest with a wand
of death. Then I left, without the Amulet. Dang! Seven levels later I
realized it and ran back down. Then I ran back up. The mysterious force
was pretty nice to me, must have been because I was chaotic. I used TC
to make my run really short since I had spare wands and scrolls of
Tele. Before leaving I prepared 4 scrolls of gold detection and went
up. By now my only remaining pet is Crossbones. Earth was easy with the
scroll same as Air, but Crossbones left me on air. Fire wasn't too
bad, I was careful to make sure my scrolls didn't get burnt. I used
the scroll on water and found the portal to be in a bubble very close.
On the Astral I took Death first, hitting him over the head with a
!oParalyze then had fun killing him. That alter was Neutral, so I
headed back to the right where Pestilence is. Get him with the /oD. The
alter is Chaotic so I sacrifice the Amulet.


